   "def": "(n; pronounced in-DITE-ment) — the formal written statement of the charges. Verb to indict; adjective indictable (an offence serious enough to be tried on indictment). The register ladder is worth having whole: to accuse (general) → to charge (by police) → to indict (formally) → to arraign (to put the charges to the defendant in court).",
